; RUN: @iriec --target mos6502 --placement naive --emit=asm @file
; RUN-exec: @irie-exec @file --target mos6502-bbcmicro --emulator @emulator --exec "many_values(*, *)"

; More values than zero page has bytes: 40 chained i32 adds leave 160 byte values,
; each with a home of its own. Program layout keeps the busiest homes in zero page
; and puts the rest in absolute memory, where each access is the absolute form of
; the same instruction (`LDA abs`, `ADC abs`, `STA abs`).

